    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d513">

                <pb facs="0680" n="560" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg560"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Italian
                        Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-03-31"><hi rendition="#italic">March 31,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 257.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to this Department’s note
                    No. 255, of the 27th instant, I have the honor to inform you that, by the
                    President’s direction, Mr. Albert F. Woods, vegetable pathologist of the
                    Department of Agriculture, has been designated as the technical agricultural
                    associate of Ambassador White at the conference for the formulation of rules to
                    govern the international institute of agriculture, to be held at Rome in May,
                    1905.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
